{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793555334,"nonce":"vzH5iUm9rIbSIjSbYxGXyH/L93M=","title":"Portable library code was refused whole for every Python program that uses sets: go, hexiom2, meteor, raytrace, scimark, telco","message":"The machine code a snapshot carries for the library is placed all or none (CraneliftBackend::place_portable_functions): one callee whose declared signature differs from the one the code was compiled against declines the lot. ZYNTAX_TRACE_PORTABLE=1 on go, hexiom2, meteor-contest, raytrace-simple, scimark (SOR) and telco printed:\n\n  [portable] placing none: callee zb_hook_shaped_set_le of zb_any_lt is declared Some(\"(i64, i64, i8) -\u003e i8 system_v\") here, (i64, i64, i8 uext) -\u003e i8 system_v in the code\n\nThe library is compiled at build time with the hook an external declaration, and a narrow argument of an external declaration carries uext (translate_signature_for). A program that defines the hook declares it without; the caller extending an argument the callee does not ask for is safe, so the check now accepts that direction (callee_signature_accepts) and still declines the reverse and any other difference. Programs that define no such hook were placing 46 to 146 functions already (chaos, pyaes, deltablue, fannkuch, float, json_bench, nbody, nqueens, richards, spectral-norm); with the fix all of them do (go 161, hexiom2 150, raytrace 141, scimark 155, telco 129, meteor 136).\n\nEffect, NUC, 4 pinned cores, 15 interleaved runs of the six rows plus scimark lu and fft: wall 0.960, CPU 0.897, score (mean iteration) 0.986. go wall -8%, telco -9%, fft -6%, meteor -3.8%; raytrace and SOR within noise on the score. The environment-variable pitfall in 51eebdd (any ZYNTAX_* outside a short list turns portable code off) was the way this was found: the same binary was 4% slower with an unused variable set.\n\nNot placed still: meteor and scimark print `not placing #524: krio_fiber_new_with_env was None where it was compiled`, a per-function skip (the program's build has no fiber runtime symbol the library was compiled against).","files":null}]}